# UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer suppressions — VENDORED code only.
#
# libresidfp shifts negative values in its external-filter maths
# (src/third_party/libresidfp/src/ExternalFilter.h:134, "left shift of
# negative value"). Formally UB, entirely upstream, and reached by every test
# that instantiates a SID — which is most of the suite.
#
# Same reasoning as tests/tsan.supp: a nightly job that is red for a
# third-party reason is a job nobody reads, so the memory bugs it exists to
# catch in POM1's own code never surface. Suppress the vendored noise, keep
# the signal ours.
#
# Never add a POM1 file here. Undefined behaviour in our code is a bug to fix.
shift-base:third_party/libresidfp
shift-base:ExternalFilter.h
